AB  - Ultrasonography imaging, or echography, makes use of high-frequency sound waves to form photos of the human physique. Due to its non-invasive nature and ability of imaging in real-time, it has become a standard diagnostic tool in the medical field. Ultrasound is commonly used to assess fetal growth and well-being in pregnancy, but is also useful for the diagnosis of hepatic, renal, cardiac, and vascular malformations and tumors. Herein we investigate spherical gas bubbles in viscoelastic fluids subjected to an external sonic field. Additionally, (Artificial intelligence)AI enhance the mesh efficiency and make reliable while reducing manual intervention, it supports data analytics and automation, these are the few ways through which AI is changing the game of fluid dynamics. The innovative intelligent framework can serve as a computational tool to suggest a solution for improving understanding of bubble dynamics in viscoelastic fluids, which is crucial to medical ultrasound imaging and effective targeted drug delivery systems. The AI-based strategy not just improves modeling precision but additionally allows new directions for non-invasive clinical diagnoses and therapeutic approaches. Characterization of bubble dynamics in a Williamson fluid model (WFM) using artificial intelligence techniques and a NARX networks (up to non-linear autoregressive with exogenous inputs, denoted by NARX) with LMT training. The data for WFM is collected by performing NARX-LMT training of the model, where parameters are varied in a systematic manner such as Weber number, Weissenberg number, pressure acting on velocity, radius of the bubble, and so on, from the Adams numerical approach for the same. In this paper, the proposed WFM is subjected to a very comprehensive assessment consisting of iterative learning curves in terms of Mean Square Error (MSE), analysis of error histograms, investigations of adaptive control factors, as well as regression and time series response metrics for several versions of a non-linear fluid model based on bubble dynamics.
