KW  - Correlation filter
KW  - Assembly quality inspection
KW  - Confined space
KW  - Depth map
KW  - Feature fusion
KW  - Anti-Occlusion
AB  - In industrial manufacturing, assembly quality inspection in confined spaces is crucial for ensuring product reliability. Although many studies have achieved notable progress in object detection and defect identification, significant challenges remain in terms of real-time processing capability and effective occlusion handling, particularly in complex assembly environments. Therefore, aiming to address these challenges, a 3D-enhanced occlusion-aware correlation filter specifically designed for assembly quality inspection in complex confined spaces is proposed. First, a three-dimensional enhancement method that incorporates depth-aware weighting adjustments into correlation filter response maps is developed, enabling the correlation filter to perceive three-dimensional spatial information. Second, an adaptive multi-feature fusion mechanism based on response map metrics is designed to boost robustness by leveraging complementary feature strengths, ensuring higher inspection accuracy in complex environments. Finally, a region-based anti-occlusion strategy is implemented to effectively mitigate occlusion issues by dividing the sample search area into sub-regions and performing independent detection in each through local features. Comprehensive experiments demonstrate the proposed inspection method's effectiveness, achieving an overall inspection accuracy of 94.2 % for component misplacement, missing components, and improper assembly, while maintaining over 83 % accuracy under partial occlusion conditions, significantly outperforming conventional image processing approaches.
