AB  - Construction safety management is critical for identifying and controlling potential risks on-site. While monocular vision is commonly used for hazard recognition, its lack of depth information makes accurate hazard localization challenging. To enhance safety management efficiency, this study proposed a localization method for multiple construction hazards using panoramic mobile tracking. First, the true pose of the monocular camera's moving trajectory is recovered through panoramic spatial transformations. Second, numerous safety hazards are localized by clustering the intersection points of observation lines. A total of 1014 images of unsealed openings were collected from five construction projects for model training. The proposed method achieved high semantic segmentation accuracy (96.38 %) and precise spatial localization (deviation <0.8 m) of indoor unsealed openings. This research presents a monocular vision-based approach for hazard recognition and localization, offering a practical reference for intelligent construction safety inspections in large-scale spaces.
