AB  - The joint classification approach of hyperspectral image (HSI) and light detection and ranging (LiDAR) data based on deep learning (DL) has received increasing attention. However, most existing deep-learning methods insufficiently handle the modal heterogeneity between HSI and LiDAR, making it difficult to fully exploit the inherent complementarity and correlation. Furthermore, most existing methods lack the ability to model fuzzy boundaries and class uncertainty. To this end, we propose a fuzzy enhanced transformer network (FETNet) for HSI and LiDAR data classification. Specifically, we designed a fuzzy spatial attention module (FSAM). By introducing a learnable Gaussian membership function, FSAM enables dynamic quantification of local spatial correlations and adaptive weighted fusion, thus fully exploiting the complementary advantages of HSI and LiDAR data in spatial information. Subsequently, a fuzzy enhanced transformer module (FETM) is constructed, which integrates fuzzy logic into the self-attention mechanism. Through a parameterized fuzzy membership discrimination mechanism, it effectively models the uncertainty and ambiguity in multi-modal data. Finally, a fuzzy learning module (FLM) is introduced. Through multi-scale fuzzy modeling, FLM enables the model to more accurately capture the fuzzy transition regions between classes. The experimental results show that the proposed FETNet outperforms other state-of-the-art methods. The code of this work will be accessible at https://github.com/lplxtp/FETNet.
