AB  - The rapid growth of healthcare services has led to an unprecedented surge in the generation of medical waste, posing serious environmental and public health risks. Efficient and precise identification of medical waste is critical for intelligent waste management, yet existing detection methods struggle with complex visual scenarios characterized by small, overlapping, and multi-class objects. In this study, we propose a novel detection framework, YESG (You Only Look Once Version 11 (YOLOv11) with Efficient Channel Attention, Slide Loss Function, and Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping Plus Plus), based on YOLOv11, incorporating three key enhancements: the SlideLoss function, the Efficient Channel Attention (ECA) mechanism, and Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping Plus Plus (Grad-CAM++) for model interpretability. A dataset of medical waste was constructed with 14 waste categories, comprising 10,249 annotated images, and augmented to 26,639 samples. Experimental results show that YESG significantly outperforms baseline and other You Only Look Once variants across both single-class instance detection (SCID) and multi-class instance detection tasks (MCID). On the SCID task, YESG-m achieves a mean Average Precision (mAP) of 95.12 % an Intersection-over-Union (IoU) threshold of 0.5, mAP@74.76 % across IoU thresholds from 0.5 to 0.95, recall of 89.91 %, and precision of 93.73 %, while maintaining superior feature compactness and inter-class separability. On the more challenging MCID task, YESG-m reaches mAP of 84.47 % across IoU thresholds of 0.5 and precision of 86.87 %. These results highlight the model's effectiveness in enhancing both detection accuracy and interpretability, offering a practical solution for real-world medical waste classification and sustainable waste management.
