AB  - The digitalization of the banking services has caused issues with data breaches, identity theft, and unauthorized access to the data which is a significant issue when ensuring the safety and complete transparency of the financial transactions. Current security systems tend to be centralized authentication systems that can be compromised, suffer data leakage and single point of failure. In order to overcome these constraints, this paper offers a new Active Directory-Blockchain-Artificial Intelligence (AI) integrated architecture that balances the merits of centralized identity management, decentralized data integrity, and intelligent decision-making. The architecture uses Active Directory (AD) to authenticate users, Blockchain to record transactions in an immutable and verifiable manner and AI-assisted Machine Learning (ML) algorithms to classify these transactions intelligently. Specifically, t-distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) is used for feature extraction, while Random Forest (RF) is utilized to predict customer churn and evaluate the risk.The experimental analysis of the Bank Churn Modelling dataset proves that the proposed model has the best results with the 98.23 % accuracy, 97.88 % precision, 97.54 % recall, and 97.71 % F 1 -score results, significantly exceeding the results of existing ML and deep learning models. The findings affirm that the combined use of AD and blockchain with the AI is a powerful tool to improve the security, transparency, and predictive performance to offer a scalable tool to realize secure and intelligent banking activities.
