AB  - The rapid evolution of urban mobility demands intelligent systems capable of perceiving, understanding, and responding to complex traffic environments involving dynamic interactions between vehicles and pedestrians. Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) are increasingly relying on Artificial Intelligence (AI)-driven solutions to improve safety and efficiency. This work presents an AI-driven vehicle–pedestrian visual attention scheme designed to enhance ITS. The proposed methodology leverages an advanced deep learning-based framework to dynamically prioritize and detect vehicle–pedestrian interaction in complex urban traffic scenarios. By incorporating contextual attention mechanism, the approach improves the vehicle–pedestrian detection with better accuracy than traditional methods. The proposed scheme integrates object detection model to optimize vehicle–pedestrian interaction recognition, ensuring computational efficiency and scalability for large-scale ITS deployment. Experimental results on two benchmark datasets demonstrate the superior performance of the proposed method making it a novel approach for enhancing intelligent transportation technologies.
