AB  - The rapidly growing demand for connectivity has necessitated the efficient production of microwave (MW) filter units, where the critical step of tuning these filters often becomes a bottleneck due to its traditional manual process. This research aims to explore and evaluate various MW filter tuning techniques proposed by researchers, highlighting their limitations and providing a comparative analysis. To this end, approximately 200 research papers from various journals and conferences were systematically reviewed to gather insights into existing MW filter tuning methodologies. The review revealed that while numerous techniques exist for MW filter tuning, each has limitations that hinder its universal applicability. Many traditional methods are labor-intensive and require expert intervention, leading to inefficiencies in filter production. The paper ends with the implementation of Dezert–Smarandache Theory (DSmT) and Machine Learning (ML) based filter tuning algorithm. This approach not only addresses bottlenecks in filter production but also paves the way for future advancements in automated tuning technologies. In nutshell, the comprehensive comparative analysis provided in this paper serves as a valuable resource for researchers and practitioners seeking to enhance MW filter tuning processes.
